Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: I can certainly help you with that!

First, let’s go over what an “if” statement is.  An “if” statement is a control flow statement that allows you to execute a block of code only if a certain condition is true.  If you were to write your program in this way:

int result;

if (num > 0)
    result = 1;
else
    result = -1;

This would check whether or not the number is positive.  If it is positive, it will execute the block of code that sets the variable result to 1.  Otherwise, it will execute the block of code that sets the variable result to -1.
